s+=['','The OpenAlex candidate identifier W2535495547 and DOI 10.1090/bull/1563 were exploratory, not verified identifiers for the source; their requests returned 429. Do not count that as a successful citation search.','','## Exact source statement','Levine and Peres, Laplacian growth, sandpiles and scaling limits, arXiv:1611.00411, section 9(3), printed/PDF p. 27:','', '> Recall that the weak-∗ convergence in Theorem 6.1, proved by Pegden and Smart [60], means that the average height of the sandpile s_n in any ball converges as the lattice spacing shrinks to zero. A natural refinement would be to show that for any ball B and any integer j, the fraction of sites in B with j particles converges. Understanding the scaling limit of the sandpile identity elements (Figure 8) is another appealing problem, solved in a special case by Caracciolo, Paoletti and Sportiello [13].','','Theorem 6.1 and its preceding paragraph, p. 21: stabilize n particles at the origin in Z^d; s_n=n delta_0+Delta u_n; rescale space by n^(1/d). Thus lattice spacing is n^(-1/d), not 1/n in dimension 2. Stable heights are 0,...,2d-1. The surrounding text focuses on the square lattice. Figure 8, p. 23: Rec([0,n]^2,z), wired boundary. This is a separate family from the point-source pile.','','## Relevant references inspected','- W. Pegden and C. K. Smart, Convergence of the Abelian sandpile, Duke Mathematical Journal 162(4) (2013), 627–642; arXiv:1105.0111. Weak-* convergence; not yet a frequency theorem.','- L. Levine, W. Pegden and C. K. Smart, Apollonian structure in the Abelian sandpile, arXiv:1208.4839v2 (22 May 2014); source reference [46]. Theorem 1.3 constructs special PDE solutions, Corollary 1.4 is conditional on three preexisting quadratic regions. Page 6 says the global geometry remains a considerable challenge. It does NOT unconditionally prove an a.e. periodic-patch cover for the point-source pile.','- Andrew Melchionna, The sandpile identity element on an ellipse, arXiv:2007.05792v2 (1 July 2023). Certain ellipses E_{A,k} with A in Gamma^+; local translated-pattern agreement at most sites. A special case, not wired squares.','- W. Pegden and C. K. Smart, Stability of patterns in the Abelian sandpile, arXiv:1708.09432v2. Retrieved; theorem comparison ongoing.','- S. Caracciolo, G. Paoletti and A. Sportiello, Explicit characterization of the identity configuration in an abelian sandpile model, Journal of Physics A: Mathematical and Theoretical 41 (2008), 495003; arXiv:0809.3416. The source explicitly labels this a special case.','- arXiv:2308.12183 and arXiv:2603.12006 concern Sierpinski gasket identities, a different graph.','- arXiv:2607.26169, Scaling and partial universality of the height zero probability in the 2D Abelian sandpile, concerns the stationary random sandpile; not deterministic stabilization of n delta_0.','','## Brain and earlier attempts','Read-only math_recall on sandpile/Pegden/Smart/height frequencies; brain recall on sandpile mistakes and sandpile height fraction convergence. Memory matches mostly unrelated. Intake C0100-A001 and codex_pool team_O/w333 supplied conditional patch reduction and generic weak-* counterexample. The claim that the actual point-source limit is already proved a.e. piecewise quadratic is not supported by the inspected Apollonian theorem. Git origin/master paths are being checked read-only.']
